Subject: [PATCH] djihads-range-guard: GPU address range guards in MemoryManager (pure crash safety, unconditional)

djihads-range-guard: GPU address range guards in MemoryManager (pure crash safety, unconditional)

Ported from Djihads80/Eglantine nx2-experimental c6d2acd37 ("nx2: Ocarina of Time stability,
shader and performance fixes", #794, "guard unmapped GPU writes and GPU address ranges"),
GPL-3.0-or-later, src/video_core/memory_manager.cpp only. Co-authors per that commit.

MemoryManager::GetEntry and the page tables have no bounds check. A GPU address past the address
space (junk render-target or copy registers after a pushbuffer desync) read past them and faulted
on GPUBack; our 0407-junk-address-guard covers one caller (JoinImages -> IsContinuousRange), this
covers the shared paths:
- MemoryOperation leaves a range that starts or runs past the address space alone.
- ReadBlockImpl reads such a range as zeros (as an unmapped range reads).
- IsGranularRange, IsContinuousRange and IsFullyMappedRange answer false for it (MemoryOperation
  skipping it would otherwise leave their default "true").
- GpuToCpuAddress refuses a page-table entry that points past the 36-bit device space (logged,
  first 16), instead of handing out a pointer past the device memory manager's tables.
Unconditional: only ranges that indexed past the tables (undefined behaviour, a GPUBack fault)
change; every in-range access is byte-identical. Not ported from the same hunks: Nx2Perf bounds
(map-time continuous runs), ReadU32 page cache, FlushQueryResults plumbing.

Checks (djihads-c6d2_checks.sh, log djihads-c6d2.checks.log): git apply --check on the T82 core,
patch on a copy, prepare-vulkan-port.py same 6 anchor skips as baseline, -fsyntax-only rc=0 on
every TU the diff reaches (generated copies included), injected static_assert seen in each,
and all four djihads-*.diff stack in one tree (same anchors, rc=0). Not built, not run.

